result: 'Runtime scope layer implemented. jinn_coro_t gained `scope` ptr + atomic
  `cancelled` (jinn_rt.h, init in coro.c). NEW runtime/scope.c (added to build.rs):
  jinn_scope_t {live_children, cancelled, lock, parent coro, prev (nesting stack),
  children[], actors[]}. Thread-local tl_scope. Functions: jinn_scope_create (push),
  jinn_scope_current/set_current, jinn_scope_register_child (child->scope=cur, live++,
  inherit cancel), jinn_scope_add_actor, jinn_scope_child_done (live--, wake parent
  at 0), jinn_scope_cancel (idempotent, mark children cancelled + close owned actor
  mailboxes), jinn_scope_check_cancelled, jinn_scope_stop_actors (graceful close),
  jinn_scope_join (park parent until live==0, then pop+free). sched.c worker loop:
  sets tl_scope=coro->scope before running (so nested dispatches register), clears
  after; DESTROY path calls jinn_scope_child_done(coro->scope). All 9 scope fns declared
  in codegen support/runtime.rs. Inert until scopes created (2-6-3). Build clean (cc
  -Wall -Wextra), 11 concurrency tests pass.'
description: 'Runtime: add jinn_scope_t { atomic live_children, atomic cancelled,
  first_error slot, parked-parent coro, owned-actor list }. jinn_coro_t gains `scope`
  ptr (inherited at spawn) + `cancelled` flag. New runtime fns: jinn_scope_create,
  jinn_scope_register_child (live_children++ + set child.scope), jinn_scope_child_done
  (decrement, wake parent at zero), jinn_scope_join (park parent until live_children==0),
  jinn_scope_add_actor, jinn_scope_stop_actors (close owned mailboxes). tl_worker
  current coro carries scope; spawn/dispatch read it. DoD: runtime compiles; scope_create/register/join
  callable.'
